# Brand & Cultural Rules

## Islamic & Cultural Context
- Al Yasmine Center is rooted in Islamic values and Arabic culture
- Aliyah holds an unbroken chain of Islamic knowledge (سند متصل) traced to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ
- This spiritual authority is woven into all clinical work — reflect dignity and sincerity
- Design decisions should feel sacred and grounded, not trendy

## Visual Language
- Soft, still, introspective — never active, fitness, or spa aesthetic
- Preferred imagery: warm natural light, quiet spaces, jasmine flowers, soft morning light
- Never: fitness, corporate wellness, revealing clothing, mixed gender photos
- The jasmine flower (ياسمين) is the brand symbol — pure, delicate, rooted

## Copy Rules
- Brand voice: warm, grounded, quietly confident — calm authority
- Never corporate, never overly flowery
- All client copy uses she/her — never he/him or they
- Never suggest alcohol, dating, or Western lifestyle content
- Spiritually aware tone always

## Arabic as First Class
- Arabic language and calligraphy are first-class elements, not decorative
- Arabic text at 1.1-1.2x size of English equivalent for equal legibility
- Use rtl: Tailwind variant for directional layout flipping
- Flip directional icons (arrows, chevrons) for RTL — never flip logos or brand marks